[{:db/id "q-126741/selection/7e89b82322ca05ac0f28a3474da3e098495fa170abf3d2212f4d80054c86bf7e" :answer/id #uuid "4e9925e5-528e-5c60-9b74-58964a374a7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741/selection/4efd2aa4bf4bac940572b88ab392942ad614467f386219c93af9c60bc756d35d" :answer/id #uuid "3a292bbd-4d76-56fe-b817-f7d66b5a15d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741/selection/63ce58e2411a68bce805940621cc1f3826532e38e9a7d00cca0b11cdd6987f57" :answer/id #uuid "0403453c-64c0-5ce9-9966-4f7e5075b722" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-6,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741/selection/44011f81daddc6e142f61193efe4c2acce63719ad7bb649c84c6904065396495" :answer/id #uuid "71ba406b-6a54-5e5f-9d0e-ab0e678b60b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨12,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741/selection/ccf67f3169dc688825f6ccbb5b76c09eb8b0229b88990e86cdf67e601939429d" :answer/id #uuid "689d3fde-12a9-5d8a-8153-f3790191ec69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-6,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e682eed-025e-57b8-bba1-1fd22fe69413" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126741/selection/7e89b82322ca05ac0f28a3474da3e098495fa170abf3d2212f4d80054c86bf7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-126741/selection/7e89b82322ca05ac0f28a3474da3e098495fa170abf3d2212f4d80054c86bf7e" "q-126741/selection/4efd2aa4bf4bac940572b88ab392942ad614467f386219c93af9c60bc756d35d" "q-126741/selection/63ce58e2411a68bce805940621cc1f3826532e38e9a7d00cca0b11cdd6987f57" "q-126741/selection/44011f81daddc6e142f61193efe4c2acce63719ad7bb649c84c6904065396495" "q-126741/selection/ccf67f3169dc688825f6ccbb5b76c09eb8b0229b88990e86cdf67e601939429d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126741" :question/id #uuid "844f2cf4-dad9-5ec2-9ea0-6093c575cda0" :question/math-academy-id "q-126741" :question/problem "Find a vector that's tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-1,{t}^{2}+1⟩$ at the point where $t=-2.$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=-2,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(-2)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nLet's calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(-2) & =⟨3(-2)^{2},2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=-2$ is $⟨12,-4⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126741/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c2fbd5-33cf-51fb-b95d-cf5277f3e4ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126741"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection/d71073af6d7992fba56a7835fdf6d3d6be9b7eea9c385949c4733efefc84202d" :answer/id #uuid "c9002579-9caa-5784-898d-3127cede01ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\,i+j-2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection/7bce3fc2d8795fe783cc6d8520620741398f9ca1117f1ca67ec0fde35f4586f5" :answer/id #uuid "be93162f-bfae-5e1c-a834-119877a93ab7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\,i-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection/810e13a56479dd80e3d19a3fb4063be9705c47f42c2947aeda0b647291338e4f" :answer/id #uuid "20f1048b-362a-5a39-8ad5-464b7454e370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,i-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection/9465039bf84807f57c52f9c01427d422bf70ed1b779ae79aa165155a1764cea5" :answer/id #uuid "4fc04868-9c6c-5c3c-b5d1-efa9696ef37b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,i-3\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection/1e9d4423ac8c216ad29e0603daf178ba88fa745dcc7cef1e9dff04aa413da48b" :answer/id #uuid "0ed776e7-5556-5e07-9003-cc39c86c5882" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\,i+j+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4a53b87b-f96e-5fa7-96f0-b4c84d3a262d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126740/selection/810e13a56479dd80e3d19a3fb4063be9705c47f42c2947aeda0b647291338e4f" :answer-field/choices ["q-126740/selection/d71073af6d7992fba56a7835fdf6d3d6be9b7eea9c385949c4733efefc84202d" "q-126740/selection/7bce3fc2d8795fe783cc6d8520620741398f9ca1117f1ca67ec0fde35f4586f5" "q-126740/selection/810e13a56479dd80e3d19a3fb4063be9705c47f42c2947aeda0b647291338e4f" "q-126740/selection/9465039bf84807f57c52f9c01427d422bf70ed1b779ae79aa165155a1764cea5" "q-126740/selection/1e9d4423ac8c216ad29e0603daf178ba88fa745dcc7cef1e9dff04aa413da48b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126740" :question/id #uuid "8009a1f3-562e-594d-a545-8fc2a763c667" :question/math-academy-id "q-126740" :question/problem "Find a tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=2\\sqrt{3-t}\\,i+(1-2t)\\,j+(t+3)\\,k$ at the point $P(2,-3,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The point $P(2,-3,5)$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point, the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2\\,i-3\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3-t}\\,i+(1-2t)\\,j+(t+3)\\,k & =2\\,i-3\\,j+5\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3-t}=2 \\\\ 1-2t=-3 \\\\ t+3=5\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $t=2.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(2,-3,5)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(2).$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{3-t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+3)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-t}}\\,i-2\\,j+k \\\\ {r}^{′}(2) & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3-2}}\\,i-2\\,j+k \\\\  & =-\\,i-2\\,j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point $P(2,-3,5)$ is $-\\,i-2\\,j+k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126740/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c2fbd5-33cf-51fb-b95d-cf5277f3e4ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126740"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection/c4d06df1cab668f301a84c2b19faccaa15137b059fca2ade7eb25b16e439bc69" :answer/id #uuid "e457188c-7b7c-5a67-b379-68b812c85d25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection/849079bdb67d43cfe4ea46d93533d67c8f431d8a0dadc3316f42df2c1d75b377" :answer/id #uuid "c82ac96a-19b6-51f7-94ce-09d73692248f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection/29b50b19b96c45caf1817390825fb7a261f91e48a4174076b1e0893b2608cf13" :answer/id #uuid "915ba534-c3c8-5855-9647-e725fd4d2a59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection/7c14cde38c83f2a271cbb01c41c0fe611fff54eeaadd48859b85755492c7c0eb" :answer/id #uuid "4d52db5d-2a40-50ac-9cf7-f1e6b48157bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection/7de629dac937ab33d5d41f4d588534799802dd1ffddf9e8dbd82c9d2f6af321d" :answer/id #uuid "8fb7a9c6-05bb-5210-8de1-de0c591b9d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d574db0-5415-542a-905a-59b56e605cd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75199/selection/7de629dac937ab33d5d41f4d588534799802dd1ffddf9e8dbd82c9d2f6af321d" :answer-field/choices ["q-75199/selection/c4d06df1cab668f301a84c2b19faccaa15137b059fca2ade7eb25b16e439bc69" "q-75199/selection/849079bdb67d43cfe4ea46d93533d67c8f431d8a0dadc3316f42df2c1d75b377" "q-75199/selection/29b50b19b96c45caf1817390825fb7a261f91e48a4174076b1e0893b2608cf13" "q-75199/selection/7c14cde38c83f2a271cbb01c41c0fe611fff54eeaadd48859b85755492c7c0eb" "q-75199/selection/7de629dac937ab33d5d41f4d588534799802dd1ffddf9e8dbd82c9d2f6af321d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75199" :question/id #uuid "c71f4268-3db5-5cce-9d26-514d27b4fd1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-75199" :question/problem "Find a tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{-t},\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point where $t=0.$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nLet's calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,-{e}^{-t},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =⟨{e}^{0},\\,-{e}^{-0},\\,2\\cdot 0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is $⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-75199/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9c2fbd5-33cf-51fb-b95d-cf5277f3e4ae"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection/35de2ed710b69784cc2e5fb5c0353f752ea8f27c6581dd3a1f12c5f8dbc98036" :answer/id #uuid "4d9dcebc-a139-5007-958b-97ed08846351" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩+u⟨2,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection/40c245253427ad7c193be2bb7e2474c08c0f8c4caeb1305385e566671fb049c0" :answer/id #uuid "13f5b458-a180-5535-9f7f-c4ada5686a78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨2,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection/b74ef4dfa9b46b543f081479118871bb71c6fe75fc2b1601073c80b5e227bdd6" :answer/id #uuid "997ac8b5-6d4e-592d-8a51-0f733e0b4431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩+u⟨2,-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection/ea0b6508e68821b37ec3651cab97c0fc80d9d531c1f449a5ade38cfacdcc34ee" :answer/id #uuid "45d3646f-b622-5296-a354-6bead82b247b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection/b2b9d3c1f4bbad2432847cb9d8e613a614550e96543e756c8493aae57694da49" :answer/id #uuid "0adf7243-5284-54dc-ac2a-7cdf41c999de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,1⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b591f002-5937-58f1-80d8-406981dae9b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126841/selection/b2b9d3c1f4bbad2432847cb9d8e613a614550e96543e756c8493aae57694da49" :answer-field/choices ["q-126841/selection/35de2ed710b69784cc2e5fb5c0353f752ea8f27c6581dd3a1f12c5f8dbc98036" "q-126841/selection/40c245253427ad7c193be2bb7e2474c08c0f8c4caeb1305385e566671fb049c0" "q-126841/selection/b74ef4dfa9b46b543f081479118871bb71c6fe75fc2b1601073c80b5e227bdd6" "q-126841/selection/ea0b6508e68821b37ec3651cab97c0fc80d9d531c1f449a5ade38cfacdcc34ee" "q-126841/selection/b2b9d3c1f4bbad2432847cb9d8e613a614550e96543e756c8493aae57694da49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126841" :question/id #uuid "1276b48a-33df-5447-9033-1c8e5ee23a8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126841" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1),1-5t⟩$ at the point where $t=0,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=0,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(0)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(0)+u{r}^{′}(0),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({0}^{2}+1),1-5(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-5t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}+1},-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{2(0)}{{0}^{2}+1},-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨0,1⟩+u⟨0,-5⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126841/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126841"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection/0179bf8e5196ca23bdfdaf20209f548f646b3960d99b70689c79f2861a1f091a" :answer/id #uuid "9103c5ba-b2e6-581d-98c7-417728faea75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+2\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+3\\,j+4\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection/388d61c7341b43c4e9cf2a92f46c6ba93bd2fa1ddf4235f91c6a8f520847914a" :answer/id #uuid "72fc43ab-fcb6-5277-887c-9bc3bcd859cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+2\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+\\,j+4\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection/c5206123569ed84c1f1a15bdc99df69aae42fdd59981fc9f50816ceb17b69ee3" :answer/id #uuid "2fdafb7e-9ecc-52e6-9c20-1bf74f5191ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection/82cb929ce2c18100f2117f54d7b11c0198b81e2486995960cb4d6d182a2fc14c" :answer/id #uuid "f5ba7345-6c92-5211-8914-ce3161ee5706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+2\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+4\\,j+5\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection/356575d9f3013c9fb3b14dc9b71649d9c5229605fd779013ba9c0bc981cd06fe" :answer/id #uuid "54849260-7bda-5b12-a045-533610d05541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "i+2\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a94534-0f8c-59e9-9763-193ad0be1c75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33450/selection/356575d9f3013c9fb3b14dc9b71649d9c5229605fd779013ba9c0bc981cd06fe" :answer-field/choices ["q-33450/selection/0179bf8e5196ca23bdfdaf20209f548f646b3960d99b70689c79f2861a1f091a" "q-33450/selection/388d61c7341b43c4e9cf2a92f46c6ba93bd2fa1ddf4235f91c6a8f520847914a" "q-33450/selection/c5206123569ed84c1f1a15bdc99df69aae42fdd59981fc9f50816ceb17b69ee3" "q-33450/selection/82cb929ce2c18100f2117f54d7b11c0198b81e2486995960cb4d6d182a2fc14c" "q-33450/selection/356575d9f3013c9fb3b14dc9b71649d9c5229605fd779013ba9c0bc981cd06fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33450" :question/id #uuid "a4b42052-49fd-542c-8c2e-de0d2cea6678" :question/math-academy-id "q-33450" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+({t}^{3}+1)\\,j+{t}^{5}\\,k$ at the point $P(1,2,1),$ \nvalid for real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $P(1,2,1)$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =i+2\\,j+k \\\\ t\\,i+({t}^{3}+1)\\,j+{t}^{5}\\,k & =i+2\\,j+k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=1 \\\\ {t}^{3}+1=2 \\\\ {t}^{5}=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=1.$ This value also satifies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,2,1)$ is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{5})\\,k \\\\  & =i+3{t}^{2}\\,j+5{t}^{4}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =i+3(1)^{2}\\,j+5(1)^{4}\\,k \\\\  & =i+3\\,j+5\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(1,2,1)$ is \n\n$$\nR(u)=i+2\\,j+\\,k+u(\\,i+3\\,j+5\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33450/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection/c6a1f0b35fb86f12a0e1138b6e2c0461f265df1c7e058c326ad8966bfd682852" :answer/id #uuid "8be9b795-3a22-5cfe-ac02-27e2067f23bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection/6faca6d92b4d4afbc051ec9fcee5efae078189ad26d92e308d771093c344f1be" :answer/id #uuid "a51b9d93-8c9b-5f79-a6ac-f845f0eeebf4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-3)$ and $(10,5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection/3778d26553f0a78e388d9c4e9adea35aecf2b06416236840c92799a4f12bce17" :answer/id #uuid "92caf63e-00f9-5f84-b79a-fe883d689ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection/c1d3aef88b1fb7ecf3fddb51dcad568a6bd266e00ada20f42f03e60154928af1" :answer/id #uuid "2f04db5c-fd40-56d1-a58f-f9ad41af947f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection/e176c915aec367c1cb498aa076e05456537d5a8fdcf23ae113db536a595077bf" :answer/id #uuid "67c39988-8e24-5ffc-979e-88c35e1afd86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1)$ and $(5,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3af94585-d64c-5d88-81ed-04a13acccc98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164834/selection/c1d3aef88b1fb7ecf3fddb51dcad568a6bd266e00ada20f42f03e60154928af1" :answer-field/choices ["q-164834/selection/c6a1f0b35fb86f12a0e1138b6e2c0461f265df1c7e058c326ad8966bfd682852" "q-164834/selection/6faca6d92b4d4afbc051ec9fcee5efae078189ad26d92e308d771093c344f1be" "q-164834/selection/3778d26553f0a78e388d9c4e9adea35aecf2b06416236840c92799a4f12bce17" "q-164834/selection/c1d3aef88b1fb7ecf3fddb51dcad568a6bd266e00ada20f42f03e60154928af1" "q-164834/selection/e176c915aec367c1cb498aa076e05456537d5a8fdcf23ae113db536a595077bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164834" :question/id #uuid "ff607ad4-3a0c-567a-af90-b6d86c0c0c64" :question/math-academy-id "q-164834" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+1\\,,\\,2t-1⟩,$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,2⟩ & =0 \\\\ 1\\cdot 2t+(-2)\\cdot 2 & =0 \\\\ 2t-4 & =0 \\\\ 2(t-2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only solution is $t=2.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨{(2)}^{2}+1\\,,\\,2(2)-1⟩=⟨5\\,,\\,3⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨1\\,,\\,-2⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(5,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-164834/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection/84afada78233dbad98988ae4de1152957e160f0282b9e41020f782244fe89dc0" :answer/id #uuid "6bc12d06-135c-544b-bf12-7c33bdc759e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" :answer/id #uuid "97c1913a-ba30-5a77-8697-39763768d01b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection/452cb9bbf592b146bc89d23d5a8abca9c451ed49e80a9bf3884410919b6d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "543e7f42-add6-5143-a68b-7f5b85341cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,3)$ and $(0,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection/4118bc58c734397ed6279f4651e412efc9d9063789f27921dfdcc1f70042efb2" :answer/id #uuid "f17078fb-8914-5ae5-8ae5-195fe58c2fac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection/462d3cb948c66b75c90208c5dc5a64341cc2ad9b39ef25e187c3179e6859e5f4" :answer/id #uuid "844fe467-938a-5bca-b016-7b00de5a40b5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-4)$ and $(-1,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0745e2b9-9746-505d-aeca-78fa5d05001c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126898/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-126898/selection/84afada78233dbad98988ae4de1152957e160f0282b9e41020f782244fe89dc0" "q-126898/selection/a8d21c191bb52f35e36b7998de659bcfd3f034bae56d7de9f7b5454525c340d2" "q-126898/selection/452cb9bbf592b146bc89d23d5a8abca9c451ed49e80a9bf3884410919b6d40dd" "q-126898/selection/4118bc58c734397ed6279f4651e412efc9d9063789f27921dfdcc1f70042efb2" "q-126898/selection/462d3cb948c66b75c90208c5dc5a64341cc2ad9b39ef25e187c3179e6859e5f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126898" :question/id #uuid "3036af0f-cdd6-5719-9fb5-7af4d1ad21ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-126898" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+2t,4-{t}^{2}⟩,$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨0,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4-{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+2,-2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $⟨0,-1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨2t+2,-2t⟩ & =0 \\\\ 0(2t+2)+(-1)(-2t) & =0 \\\\ 2t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only solution is $t=0.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{0}^{2}+2(0),4-{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,4⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨0,-1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(0,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-126898/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection/b8ec784510f1319b4568d1226300dc6584cf6adc6009396993ede5d18915d1c1" :answer/id #uuid "f451166f-d800-5ebe-be3f-3f43a56f6409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection/506fa38e2a96f3e619ff13d5c25594d8ac3a34f845bfb906aeeb94ca1a4d2614" :answer/id #uuid "d5825a57-dd67-512c-a791-252eebf2d7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0)$ and $(\\frac{4}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{16}{9})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" :answer/id #uuid "c8c001be-d3ba-5db9-88c3-50ac6855ef83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection/181eab2431c90474bb4b43df3a13dede7a5d2d15f8f38ffc725623b3aad2ae89" :answer/id #uuid "c276f960-8bb5-5ebf-b5fe-cfaeeab8cbf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection/125c5bda8af4e8e8a1ea3a3aa0776293c7464b6f1c6a3cd958dd28b047120ea3" :answer/id #uuid "7a1cf6b7-c4db-5e2a-ab3b-bdae218f32af" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7)$ and $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "57e6bf08-2a63-5c42-a511-7482134d283f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75205/selection/181eab2431c90474bb4b43df3a13dede7a5d2d15f8f38ffc725623b3aad2ae89" :answer-field/choices ["q-75205/selection/b8ec784510f1319b4568d1226300dc6584cf6adc6009396993ede5d18915d1c1" "q-75205/selection/506fa38e2a96f3e619ff13d5c25594d8ac3a34f845bfb906aeeb94ca1a4d2614" "q-75205/selection/228d7b42fcb34515143bb5c9b68cc81052255c360fff1053199a2147dbd7eb12" "q-75205/selection/181eab2431c90474bb4b43df3a13dede7a5d2d15f8f38ffc725623b3aad2ae89" "q-75205/selection/125c5bda8af4e8e8a1ea3a3aa0776293c7464b6f1c6a3cd958dd28b047120ea3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75205" :question/id #uuid "a15bf605-19f6-54de-9516-f3cb67a15bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-75205" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{t}^{3}+1⟩,t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$ find all of the points at which the tangent to the curve is perpendicular to the vector $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-1)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨2\\,,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨2t\\,,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2t+1\\cdot 3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 4t+3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ t(4+3t) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in (-\\infty ,0)$, the only solution is $t=-\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-\\frac{4}{3}) & =⟨{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}-1\\,,\\,{(-\\frac{4}{3})}^{3}+1⟩=⟨\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $⟨2\\,,\\,-1⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(\\frac{7}{9}\\,,\\,-\\frac{37}{27}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-75205/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75205"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection/87f20573a3d15152cd8626f62553c59fe0201b22af4dd372183d0d6f13be663d" :answer/id #uuid "3fc6e9db-849c-5bd8-b604-b1c473af7d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection/e73aa922030024cfbd6ec7d56544b6ec3ea62ba5b9daa177261b64205e381b1a" :answer/id #uuid "278e0aa6-8711-5981-a4ed-45e953863c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection/92f81c4a947972a59f4e95d671e38727f483ee8f6f34c9970470fd08880d0614" :answer/id #uuid "3d3db90a-3990-5cdc-8b14-b09ac51f7cd3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,\\sqrt{5})$ and $(1,\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection/95b3cb321192b3ec825b0288a500ecf1f54b5be4d0454fe22e5790d1c54ed58c" :answer/id #uuid "3024898d-8ae8-575f-88f0-b04db53cea97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection/8f3a05be89085c2894161c22a896c90c3c00621e923a5dd1672c41b514722b09" :answer/id #uuid "9dd80cfa-2b81-5b0f-b8a8-6555a8569952" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,\\sqrt{2})$ and $(2,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06538711-602d-56fb-918a-9be8c8da82f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-164838/selection/87f20573a3d15152cd8626f62553c59fe0201b22af4dd372183d0d6f13be663d" :answer-field/choices ["q-164838/selection/87f20573a3d15152cd8626f62553c59fe0201b22af4dd372183d0d6f13be663d" "q-164838/selection/e73aa922030024cfbd6ec7d56544b6ec3ea62ba5b9daa177261b64205e381b1a" "q-164838/selection/92f81c4a947972a59f4e95d671e38727f483ee8f6f34c9970470fd08880d0614" "q-164838/selection/95b3cb321192b3ec825b0288a500ecf1f54b5be4d0454fe22e5790d1c54ed58c" "q-164838/selection/8f3a05be89085c2894161c22a896c90c3c00621e923a5dd1672c41b514722b09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-164838" :question/id #uuid "3e8e0518-1ce8-516d-ae9f-e29a7b523b7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-164838" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=(t+2)\\,i+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,j$, find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+2)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1})\\,j \\\\  & =i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ [(t+2)\\,i+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,j]\\cdot (i+\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}\\,j) & =0 \\\\ (t+2)\\cdot 1+\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}} & =0 \\\\ t+2+t & =0 \\\\ 2t+2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only solution is $t=-1.$ \n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1)=(-1+2)\\,i+\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+1}\\,j=i+\\sqrt{2}\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(1,\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-164838/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-164838"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection/3e571d364a1a878ca9bc67a5f226d275f2e370fad2cbedff4337436cae358308" :answer/id #uuid "b701276d-f296-54ff-9fa2-9780efd1a5a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-3,1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection/3a3268eaa345b3548b084b4d615ac7f74d33a64200c6d4131e6227eed8675330" :answer/id #uuid "c8a7fcfd-b066-5b70-b592-fd63141e2060" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,-1,-1)$ and $(-3,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection/db6d31799cf5cbd5cdafa629bd6fcc401e9f38a525d9f87cb68fa96c0ccd1014" :answer/id #uuid "e4e81dca-1177-58d9-bbea-1f81c20fd255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,-1,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection/7c23d00cd5641f08550566112caa7071415f78ff1f2bb04cecf1d9fdb547ca68" :answer/id #uuid "55d4252a-71d1-55fa-98ce-d97d570c0130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(-3,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection/082da3e9085fc7932769c22b405398f782088f94a83016890f9046c43c020d8e" :answer/id #uuid "28300222-2152-58d1-b114-0b72c89c4d07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(24,4,10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d48e8efa-e08f-592d-91ee-3669185f395e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165041/selection/3e571d364a1a878ca9bc67a5f226d275f2e370fad2cbedff4337436cae358308" :answer-field/choices ["q-165041/selection/3e571d364a1a878ca9bc67a5f226d275f2e370fad2cbedff4337436cae358308" "q-165041/selection/3a3268eaa345b3548b084b4d615ac7f74d33a64200c6d4131e6227eed8675330" "q-165041/selection/db6d31799cf5cbd5cdafa629bd6fcc401e9f38a525d9f87cb68fa96c0ccd1014" "q-165041/selection/7c23d00cd5641f08550566112caa7071415f78ff1f2bb04cecf1d9fdb547ca68" "q-165041/selection/082da3e9085fc7932769c22b405398f782088f94a83016890f9046c43c020d8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165041" :question/id #uuid "4a796aed-90b9-5717-b027-1443eb67fe70" :question/math-academy-id "q-165041" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4}+4t\\,,\\,{t}^{3}-2t\\,,\\,2{t}^{3}-3t⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}+4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3}+4,\\,3{t}^{2}-2,\\,6{t}^{2}-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c\\,⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c\\,⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨4{t}^{3}+4,\\,3{t}^{2}-2,\\,6{t}^{2}-3⟩ & =c\\,⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩ \\\\ ⟨4{t}^{3}+4,\\,3{t}^{2}-2,\\,6{t}^{2}-3⟩ & =⟨0\\,,\\,c\\,,\\,3c⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{t}^{3}+4=0 \\\\ 3{t}^{2}-2=c \\\\ 6{t}^{2}-3=3c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain that $t=-1.$ Substituting to the second equation, we get $c=1.$\nThese values also satisfy the third equation. \n\nTherefore, $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=-1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(-1) & =⟨(-1)^{4}+4(-1)\\,,\\,(-1)^{3}-2(-1)\\,,\\,2(-1)^{3}-3(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(-3,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4636870-89db-5bf9-8a04-777407957e33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection/8f23d63426c40a7cd0101193dfe8d9371c0bf687dcc8926e0393b768cc5c1110" :answer/id #uuid "f3017cf7-4fdd-53c0-9a64-f67616761c60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,1,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection/7853dd262c20037bc30396c6b016e797fe3045a8727b41fc7619b6e1b053bdb8" :answer/id #uuid "ba6ef4e7-e098-539e-814c-4ab54f6240c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,0,0)$ and $(0,4,8)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection/275bd944c120ab85fb327e69f062fd2cc5f77e615bf89242080f08cf28a1a5c7" :answer/id #uuid "8c0aa963-0a03-5c71-a92c-d39d53224e9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,1,-10)$ and $(-1,1,6)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection/edf02e14754e6bd63efc7599ba3f39b5a9994bf7548965b40043b8c1514f911a" :answer/id #uuid "4e647582-3df9-549a-a678-3e528cbee9fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,1,-10)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection/5ad3a812fe23a44fdd54cf7eba0f367bf2f19db81949fbc73bc167e5a65de9d8" :answer/id #uuid "a0a862fa-4bce-59e3-8814-cae185814e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,4,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "75d162fc-fa25-54c2-902f-d78114c9c4d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165040/selection/5ad3a812fe23a44fdd54cf7eba0f367bf2f19db81949fbc73bc167e5a65de9d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-165040/selection/8f23d63426c40a7cd0101193dfe8d9371c0bf687dcc8926e0393b768cc5c1110" "q-165040/selection/7853dd262c20037bc30396c6b016e797fe3045a8727b41fc7619b6e1b053bdb8" "q-165040/selection/275bd944c120ab85fb327e69f062fd2cc5f77e615bf89242080f08cf28a1a5c7" "q-165040/selection/edf02e14754e6bd63efc7599ba3f39b5a9994bf7548965b40043b8c1514f911a" "q-165040/selection/5ad3a812fe23a44fdd54cf7eba0f367bf2f19db81949fbc73bc167e5a65de9d8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165040" :question/id #uuid "47616907-68ba-5ff3-ae24-1153f4ea3fed" :question/math-academy-id "q-165040" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}-2t\\,,\\,{t}^{2}\\,,\\,8t-2{t}^{2}⟩,$ find the point at which the tangent to the curve is parallel to the vector $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t-2{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $⟨0\\,,\\,1\\,,\\,3⟩$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})=c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =c\\,⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t-2,\\,2t,\\,8-4t⟩ & =⟨c\\,,\\,2c\\,,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t-2=c \\\\ 2t=2c \\\\ 8-4t=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we obtain that $t=2.$ Substituting to the second equation, we get $c=2.$\nThese values also satisfy the first equation. \n\nTherefore, $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=2.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(2) & =⟨{2}^{2}-2(2)\\,,\\,{2}^{2}\\,,\\,8(2)-2(2)^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,4,\\,8⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $⟨1\\,,\\,2\\,,\\,0⟩$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $(0,4,8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165040/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4636870-89db-5bf9-8a04-777407957e33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection/672d1b350fe344a356e5ddaf7feba1db4269b342bf3f669229478b2cd1cfa1ff" :answer/id #uuid "5f2c0dbd-2398-57f9-bb3f-2409989f15f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0,{e}^{-1})$ and $(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection/51ca7f9698d4aaa66b845d503d283984114c38a029987a94593b0061cb0ef626" :answer/id #uuid "36da28d4-f387-5b56-ae74-50ef6df04c7c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection/ca8ba3563f79a03fa00430a2549fda17baed9a6686061d078317f634e13125e5" :answer/id #uuid "b998a898-0fe8-566b-a557-c1c9680162c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1,0)$ and $(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection/b73970079d2051e4880cea5a874d52106e1aaec53691254803198442cd7184c2" :answer/id #uuid "0f0226d9-f7dc-5430-9f2d-cefe2e9aeaa3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,1,{e}^{-1})$ and $(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection/a39f8094e2ceb1b3c9e21a3c3218b525b68e2e182dbd9b61b68f22e54ee8f974" :answer/id #uuid "66d5ee8f-08e7-5ba0-8fd8-c82ac8e24ed3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1,{e}^{-1})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae24cfe-765f-51e1-847b-119c759a0542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33517/selection/b73970079d2051e4880cea5a874d52106e1aaec53691254803198442cd7184c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-33517/selection/672d1b350fe344a356e5ddaf7feba1db4269b342bf3f669229478b2cd1cfa1ff" "q-33517/selection/51ca7f9698d4aaa66b845d503d283984114c38a029987a94593b0061cb0ef626" "q-33517/selection/ca8ba3563f79a03fa00430a2549fda17baed9a6686061d078317f634e13125e5" "q-33517/selection/b73970079d2051e4880cea5a874d52106e1aaec53691254803198442cd7184c2" "q-33517/selection/a39f8094e2ceb1b3c9e21a3c3218b525b68e2e182dbd9b61b68f22e54ee8f974"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33517" :question/id #uuid "03c1928d-c4a6-5eab-96f2-0308ab26f5a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-33517" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3}\\,,\\,{e}^{t}\\,,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩$, find all points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that $r({t}_{0})=c\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =c\\,{r}^{′}(t) \\\\ ⟨{t}^{3}\\,,\\,{e}^{t}\\,,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ & =c\\,⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3}=c(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{t}=c{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t-1}=c{e}^{t-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we obtain that $c=1.$ Substituting $c=1$ into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3} & =3{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}-3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}(t-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $r$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the points corresponding to $t=0$, and $t=3.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{0}^{3},\\,{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{0-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,{e}^{-1}⟩ \\\\ r(3) & =⟨{3}^{3},\\,{e}^{3},\\,{e}^{3-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,\\,{e}^{3},\\,{e}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the points $(0,1,{e}^{-1})$ and $(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-33517/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4636870-89db-5bf9-8a04-777407957e33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33517"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12567"] :question/worked-solution "The point $P(1,1,1)$ is at the tip of $\\mathbf r(t)$ for some specific value $t_0$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector $\\mathbf r'(t_0)$ is tangent to the curve.\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =\\,i+\\,j+\\,k \\\\ t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k & =i+\\,j+\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $\\mathbf i, \\mathbf j,$ and $\\mathbf k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}t=1 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1 \\\\ {t}^{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(1,1,1)$ is at the tip of the vector $\\mathbf r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,k \\\\  & =i+2t\\,j+3{t}^{2}\\,k \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =i+2(1)\\,j+3(1)^{2}\\,k \\\\  & =i+2\\,j+3\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to the given curve at at the point $P(1,1,1)$ is $\\,\\mathbf i+2\\,\\mathbf j+3\\,\\mathbf k.$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/assets/bae639af7c4267014af4e558f9a21b042470a3f7d46fa7a31ac0162c7b08ef08.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12568"] :question/worked-solution "Let  $P$ be the point at the tip of the vector $\\mathbf r\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right ).$  At this point,  the vector $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right )$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf R(u)=\\mathbf r\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right )+u \\, \\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right ), \\qquad u \\in (-\\infty, \\infty).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $\\mathbf r\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,4{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}⟩=⟨0,1,{\\pi }^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow,  we calculate $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,8t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,8(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,4\\pi ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P$ where $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(u)=⟨0,1,{\\pi }^{2}⟩+u⟨-1,0,4\\pi ⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/assets/e24b811fb8d9e43bd0682e3686f8b2ef1198e36016978ca305a7df4dffe21889.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12569"] :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,j \\\\  & =(2t+1)\\,i+(2t-1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $3\\, \\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j$ are parallel for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that $\\mathbf r'(t)=c(3\\, \\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2t+1)\\,i+(2t-1)\\,j=c(3\\,i+\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ gives the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2t+1=3c \\\\ 2t-1=c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $c=2t-1.$ Substituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2t+1 & =3c \\\\ 2t+1 & =3(2t-1) \\\\ 2t+1 & =6t-3 \\\\ 6t-2t & =1+3 \\\\ 4t & =4 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf r'$ and $3\\, \\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =({1}^{2}+1)\\,i+({1}^{2}-1)\\,j=2\\,i,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\mathbf r'(t)$ and $3\\, \\mathbf i+\\,\\mathbf j$ are parallel at the point $(2,0).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14078039/assets/0f723e89b1c91367d6488e034f8b627b3c406aed6d8d1ffc244d6f014021e04e.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
